{"h":3396,"lines":[{"y":0.032183016988646118,"c":1,"w":0.085627517700195388,"h":0.018722200562170443,"t":"Reading","x":0.83901872579363079},{"c":1,"w":0.31102185567220053,"y":0.075097187618318739,"t":"READING PASSAGE 3","h":0.01847743538720592,"x":0.084191040028282677},{"h":0.025435353336401678,"c":1,"x":0.084122082359844988,"y":0.11182870595352856,"w":0.82763270060221361,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading"},{"c":1,"y":0.13074204919056553,"h":0.01751376490149259,"x":0.082304523832436804,"t":"Passage 3 below.","w":0.17078189849853515},{"h":0.041215049644802715,"c":1,"w":0.76037765502929699,"x":0.1229185134568118,"t":"Plant 'thermometer' triggers springtime growth by","y":0.16191742705392431},{"y":0.1990577150745052,"c":1,"w":0.3991769663492839,"h":0.024779493873335556,"x":0.30452674305124938,"t":"measuring night-time heat"},{"x":0.1047487176203534,"h":0.023746583711693803,"y":0.23663632049713457,"c":1,"t":"A photoreceptor molecule in plant cells has been found to have a second job","w":0.79048599243164064},{"w":0.77819437662760416,"c":1,"h":0.023475595301256313,"t":"as a thermometer after dark - allowing plants to read seasonal temperature","x":0.11092306600399639,"y":0.25448023935876185},{"h":0.024886959152311539,"t":"changes. Scientists say the discovery could help breed crops that are more","x":0.11096114296722134,"c":1,"y":0.27106783913015198,"w":0.77809132893880206},{"c":1,"h":0.024468533141874138,"t":"resilient to the temperatures expected to result from climate change","x":0.14998422460489261,"y":0.28970662115376733,"w":0.70004435221354167},{"c":1,"y":0.32656906517470086,"t":"A An international team of scientists led by the University of Cambridge has","x":0.077963238370025084,"w":0.7432495625813802,"h":0.024241275585161093},{"w":0.72485921223958327,"h":0.027298666703546526,"x":0.1252621320215199,"c":1,"y":0.34373245841355748,"t":"discovered that the 'thermometer' molecule in plants enables them to develop"},{"t":"according to seasonal temperature changes. Researchers have revealed that","h":0.023474519188187881,"x":0.12529419934903255,"y":0.36600666819807637,"w":0.70206715901692707,"c":1},{"h":0.022948531295722496,"c":1,"x":0.12537664273516194,"y":0.38461839179233004,"t":"molecules called phytochromes - used by plants to detect light during the day -","w":0.74720479329427092},{"x":0.12531794984094857,"t":"actually change their function in darkness to become cellular temperature gauges","y":0.40476112174796364,"h":0.023035781824406243,"w":0.75757832845052087,"c":1},{"t":"that measure the heat of the night.","w":0.32098765055338541,"x":0.12345679488791622,"h":0.018991219842953377,"y":0.4243227330173811,"c":1},{"x":0.12527978324901046,"w":0.74526346842447921,"h":0.024843128325661157,"y":0.45286946953015361,"c":1,"t":"The new findings, published in the journal Science, show that phytochromes control"},{"c":1,"x":0.12329228758305599,"w":0.78844482421874995,"t":"genetic switches in response to temperature as well as light to dictate plant development.","y":0.47197871283420234,"h":0.023428772026574229},{"y":0.50122720912090479,"w":0.72248977661132807,"h":0.022150688935224871,"c":1,"x":0.1233170799520667,"t":"At night, these molecules change states, and the pace at which they change is"},{"y":0.51879133500786356,"c":1,"w":0.76183024088541662,"t":"'directly proportional to temperature', say scientists, who compare phytochromes","h":0.025726432935087917,"x":0.12112329563048974},{"h":0.030047864880241693,"t":"to mercury in a thermometer. The warmer it is, the faster the molecular change -","c":1,"x":0.12109150740685606,"y":0.53522330372646121,"w":0.75781168619791672},{"t":"stimulating plant growth.","h":0.017667844522968212,"x":0.12139917826373212,"c":1,"y":0.55948174311460674,"w":0.24074073791503905},{"w":0.018518517812093099,"h":0.013081395583944722,"t":"C","x":0.076131687493130429,"y":0.58720930211458922,"c":1},{"h":0.023066227511887916,"x":0.11914850985894816,"w":0.76580474853515623,"c":1,"y":0.58710525693280768,"t":"Farmers and gardeners have known for hundreds of years how responsive plants are"},{"w":0.76178482055664065,"y":0.6048096434772483,"h":0.024661058531492697,"c":1,"t":"to temperature: warm winters cause many trees and flowers to bud early, something","x":0.12117429410063911},{"t":"humans have long used to predict weather and harvest times for the coming year. The","y":0.62392718224822785,"x":0.12115887940177771,"w":0.77824066162109362,"h":0.025032342252517825,"c":1},{"h":0.023678333655403394,"x":0.11917769699475116,"c":1,"w":0.78223821004231775,"y":0.64295126394676572,"t":"latest research pinpoints for the first time a molecular mechanism in plants that reacts"},{"h":0.021984711412265878,"y":0.66484830407233475,"x":0.11924473844122521,"c":1,"t":"to temperature - often triggering the buds of spring we long to see at the end of winter.","w":0.79445053100585949},{"w":0.76589635213216156,"c":1,"x":0.075877213633994522,"h":0.023293161560705711,"t":"D With weather and temperatures set to become ever more unpredictable due to","y":0.69174202444586974},{"h":0.023453933751765632,"w":0.76783721923828119,"y":0.71143945059821323,"c":1,"x":0.11917593553344669,"t":"climate change, researchers say the discovery that this light-sensing molecule also"},{"t":"functions as the internal thermometer in plant cells could help us breed tougher","y":0.72942662733308627,"w":0.74325281778971353,"h":0.023891918510374088,"x":0.12114370852435835,"c":1},{"y":0.74880367830773276,"w":0.73081776936848963,"h":0.024793544000955903,"t":"crops. 'It is estimated that agricultural yields will need to double by 2050, but","c":1,"x":0.11916492690505322},{"y":0.76914618952559177,"h":0.022854366909067503,"x":0.11918414619631941,"w":0.78220672607421871,"c":1,"t":"climate change is a major threat to achieving this. Key crops such as wheat and rice"},{"x":0.11914280483752103,"w":0.74735977172851564,"h":0.024673704544983965,"y":0.78707340497798839,"t":"are sensitive to high temperatures. Thermal stress reduces crop yields by around","c":1},{"t":"10% for every one degree increase in temperature,' says lead researcher Dr Philip","x":0.12118616917977325,"w":0.75765538533528654,"h":0.024402265694733916,"c":1,"y":0.80649961888860311},{"x":0.12131061086585058,"h":0.02126555336097391,"t":"Wigge from Cambridge's Sainsbury Laboratory. 'Discovering the molecules that","y":0.82844369340849056,"w":0.7532590738932291,"c":1},{"t":"allow plants to sense temperature has the potential to accelerate the breeding of","w":0.74318074544270829,"h":0.023768785564301287,"y":0.8471341784478772,"x":0.1191502947113157,"c":1},{"h":0.020807866072907411,"x":0.11923654599689233,"w":0.48989156087239588,"y":0.86739378768089603,"c":1,"t":"crops resilient to thermal stress and climate change?"},{"w":0.026748971939086874,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"x":0.88271604890699984,"t":"69","y":0.90843023238112497},{"y":0.9556315279170291,"c":1,"w":0.25425661722819015,"h":0.027004518273019973,"t":"IELTSXpress.com","x":0.71953327191129191}],"w":2400}